    "background_story": "Crew was a talented but temperamental artist known for his explosive outbursts in the studio. His sensitivity to criticism often made him come across as touchily defensive, but deep down, he was just passionate about his craft. Crew's emotions simmered just below the surface, and even the slightest suggestion that his work wasn't perfect could send him into a tailspin. Despite this, his colleagues admired his dedication and respected his boundaries. One day, a prominent art critic published a scathing review of Crew's latest exhibition, calling his work 'self-indulgent'. Crew was devastated, but instead of lashing out, he poured his emotions into a new piece that would become his masterpiece. The art world took notice, and Crew's reputation as a visionary artist was solidified.",
